From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nft_flow_offload: handle MediaTek WDMA paths

The BPI-R4 Pro 8X vendor tree carries a MediaTek patch that teaches
nft_flow_offload to keep the correct source MAC when the forwarding path
contains DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA. Without it, RelayD/Wi-Fi WDMA paths can populate
an incorrect source MAC and stall fastpath/hardware-path traffic.

Vendor source:
refs/vendor/bpi-r4pro-8x-openwrt24.10/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.6/
999-3015-netfilter-add-DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA-path-to-nft_flow_offload.patch

Adapted for ImmortalWrt 25.12 / Linux 6.12 by OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5).

Signed-off-by: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@local>
---
 net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c
@@ -160,6 +160,10 @@ static void nft_dev_path_info(const stru
 			}
 			info->xmit_type = FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT;
 			break;
+		case DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA:
+			if (is_zero_ether_addr(info->h_source))
+				memcpy(info->h_source, path->dev->dev_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+			break;
 		default:
 			info->indev = NULL;
 			break;
